:"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-07-25T15:53:55Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T10:48:26Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T10:39:30Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.stable.arch_linux [5b4e0cb0f]\n\n\n### System information\n\nLinux 7.1.3-arch2-2 (x86_64)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen an inner class is named after a global class, you receive a compile error.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gd\n#settings.gd\nextends Node\nclass_name Settings\n\n# Called when the node enters the scene tree for the first time.\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tpass # Replace with function body.\n\n\n# Called every frame. 'delta' is the elapsed time since the previous frame.\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tpass\n```\n\n```\n#foo.gd\nextends Node\nclass_name Foo\n\nclass Settings: # error here\n\tvar foo: int = 0\n\n# Called when the node enters the scene tree for the first time.\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tpass # Replace with function body.\n\n\n# Called every frame. 'delta' is the elapsed time since the previous frame.\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tpass\n\n```\n\nError is\n`Error at (4, 7): Class \"Settings\" hides a global script class.`\n\nThis is an error that breaks Some Addons/Plugins, since a plugin I use has an inner class `Settings` in a script and I have a Global Class `Settings`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nsee *Steps to reproduce* ","closed_by":{"login":"Raildex","id":14938934,"node_id":"MD